{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/423961-healing-kith","id":423961,"title":"Healing Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T04:20:31-08:00","id":423961,"title":"Healing Kith","content":"Mine playeress wants to play Spring Courtier that was dedicated for healing others in Arcadia. She want's to go with faith healer/shaman kind of thing, but in CtL corebook there is only Chirugeon Kith for this kind of things. Are there some alternatives, more suited for this character idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:00:18-08:00","id":424096,"title":"","content":"Just take the Spring Contracts that deal with healing; the kith can be anything from a Fairest Bright One to a Witchtooth Ogre, since being a faith healer has little to do with the actual Medicine skill (unlike the Chirurgeon kith).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:16:23-08:00","id":424123,"title":"","content":"What Contracts are about Healing, precisly? And character were healer in Arcadia - now it's more &quot;wild party goer, because I'm free of Fae and parents, yeah!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:09:56-08:00","id":424274,"title":"","content":"One of the Spring Contacts has a healing clause in the 1e core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:10:59-08:00","id":424275,"title":"","content":"Warmth of Blood, third clause of Eternal Spring. The best magical healing changelings have. Stone has a self only heal and there are two or three goblin contracts floating around but their cost is pretty steep.Another option is taking the Fairie Healing from &quot;Rights of Spring&quot; and focus more on goblin fruit healing, though it's fairly limited in the damage it can undo. However, it does offer variety in the effects of using other fruits.<br /> <br /> As for kiths it's all about how you fluff them. I will say that there is nothing wrong with Chirgueon kith being a playing as shaman/faith healer and it's blessing offers the most by way of enhancing healing. If that just isn't their cup of tea, start broadening the view of other kiths and seemings.<br /> <br /> They could be a totemic shaman and be a beast. Truefriends can add dice to any roll another person makes including resistance to diseases and toxins.<br /> <br /> Chimera might be played as someone who dealt with the strange spirit hobgoblins and made deals to get the help and medicine they needed.<br /> <br /> A Roteater could have wandered through plague infested lands, cleansing wounds by literally eating away the diseased flesh and using whatever was on hand to for cures.<br /> <br /> Darkling have Gravewights. Being a healer means being exposed to a lot of death. Plus dealing with spirits of the deceased is another shaman thing.<br /> <br /> Elementals have a close connection to nature and so have a shamanistic vibe and different elements having associations with healing, health and strength. Fire, Water, Earth, and Plants. Plus a contract of Elements or Communion with Blood could be pretty cool.<br /> <br /> The are the Weisse Frau of the Fairest kith who focus on protecting others (especially children).<br /> <br /> Witchtooth was mentioned but there's also Farwalkers that can represent wandering healers or wise hermits that people had to climb mountains to reach with the ill to get them healed.<br /> <br /> Woodwalker has that kind of vibe to but located in forests.<br /> <br /> Could be a Brewer of potions (see Faerie Healing) and with no anesthetic needed to get your patients inebriated to withstand the pain of surgery. Goes well with the party goer upon return to the mortal world.<br /> <br /> And lastly Oracle, mostly as another kith that could fit into the shaman category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:37:23-08:00","id":424607,"title":"","content":"What exactly is it about the Chirugeon kith that prevents it from being more like the concept you wish? Yes, the accompanying picture shows it to be a cross with a Grey Alien and a modern Surgeon, but that is merely one possibility. From what I can see in the Kith description, they are masters of medicine... but how that medicine is performed is not specified. You could be just as brilliant performing Holistic Healing (as used by many Asian philosophies)... or even as Psychic Surgery that is claimed to be performed by some mystics (most who are actually charlatans of some sort), though in this Fae's case, it actually works.<br /> <br /> Besides the Eternal Spring 3 contract there are some Merits that could also help with this contract (Both from Rites of Spring). The first is Faerie Healing (2 dots) that allows the character to heal others with Goblin Fruit as effectively as the character heals himself with said fruit. The second is Arcadian Metabolism (3 dots) which enhances the healing benefits the character gets from Goblin Fruits (can heal even Aggravated damage)... and combined with the previous merit can do so with others. Both of these Merits would also benefit from the Harvest (Hedge Bounty) merit too... giving you a reliable supply of Goblin Fruit to heal with. Exactly how you heal with these merits is also up to you, with a few suggestions in the Faerie Healing write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:05:57-08:00","id":425587,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you can't combine Arcadian Metabolism with Faerie Healing. <br /> <br /> And the bigger problem with Chirugeon kith is that it only operates in conjunction with mundane healing skills. It's good for being a back-alley mob doctor, but not good for combat healing using contracts like Warmth of Blood. (It's not even good for healing if you are a real doctor, as it only helps you if you have no access to proper equipment.)<br /> <br /> I mean, if you really want, you can just create a kith that has a 9-again on medicine rolls, and spend a point of glamour to get a further +2 to medicine (which would include the healing contracts). That's generally in the same league of power as a few other kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:20:19-08:00","id":425755,"title":"","content":"I've seen nothing in any of the official books that would say that Arcadian Metabolism and Faerie Healing can't be combined. Of course it does use up a lot of one's beginning Merit dots.<br /> <br /> So you want a kith that can heal with but a touch? That sort of healing isn't common in any kind of kith (most of which enhance mundane skills with their blessings). Whether medicine is done with a scalpel, herbs or some other method... it still performed in the game with the same basic mechanics. A Shaman may be more inclined toward the mystical/herbal than western medicine, but they would still use the same skills to accomplish it. Medicine on it's own doesn't actually heal a person... that takes time and rest. At best, it provides a single extra health level healed per day.<br /> <br /> Truth is that one is not likely to do much healing in the middle of combat to begin with. Such a level of healing would be the result of magic more powerful than what kith blessings can provide. Look at what it takes to heal with Eternal Spring 3... 1 Glamour and 1 Willpower to convert Lethal to Bashing and heal Bashing damage equal to the successes rolled on a Wits + Medicine + Mantle (Spring) roll. No kith blessing will be able to match this... such blessings are just too weak to provide this level of healing. What kind of Mechanic would you give such a power? Spend 1 Glamour to make a medicine roll and heal that many levels of Bashing damage (maybe exchange 2 successes to downgrade 1 lethal to bashing)? Even this is pushing the limits and making it almost as powerful as a 3 dot contract.<br /> <br /> To be honest... any amount of healing that a Kith Blessing would enable would be fairly minor... and hardly enough to make a big difference in combat. A combat healer will be relying more on powerful Contracts like Eternal Spring 3 than on a meager blessing from one's kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:33:42-08:00","id":425761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/423961-healing-kith?p=425755#post425755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen nothing in any of the official books that would say that Arcadian Metabolism and Faerie Healing can't be combined. Of course it does use up a lot of one's beginning Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faerie Healing's own description says that it only works for healing 1 lethal or 2 bashing. It's worded such that you can't use it to mix effects of unusual goblin fruit or oddments on other players who aren't Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:59:35-08:00","id":425796,"title":"","content":"Faerie Healing actually says that the one who possess it can heal others (including mortals and normal animals) as effectively with Goblin Fruit as they can themselves. It is also unique to each character that possesses it... thus if a particular changeling gets additional benefits from goblin fruit (as per the Arcadian Healing), then they can pass that additional benefit on to the one they are healing.<br /> <br /> This of course may also depend on the method of applying the healing. If The changeling has to eat the fruit then lay his hands on another... then it stands to reason that the changeling can confer the same benefit as he would receive due to Arcadian Body (since he actually ate the fruit and is using the healing it provides him to heal another). However... if the changeling feeds the fruit directly to the patient... then, yes, only the normal benefit would apply as the changeling isn't changing the fruit in any way.<br /> <br /> No one is saying that it mixes the effects of goblin fruits or oddments... it is merely taking advantage of the changeling's ability to draw more healing from goblin fruit than other changeling normally can and then pass that on to others. Yes... it is taking advantage of a loophole... but then that is the very nature of Changelings... to take advantage of such loopholes. Of course Arcadian Metabolism has its own drawback as well... namely that the character requires the very goblin fruit he uses to heal others to survive himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:48:02-08:00","id":425863,"title":"","content":"The effect (and balance) of the merit is based upon not passing any other benefit onto others than 1 lethal and 2 bashing. <br /> <br /> The description of Arcadian Metabolism makes it clear that it's a specific metabolic hypersensitivity to the goblin fruits possessed by that one individual severe enough that it alters their physiology (hence a -1 to medicine rolls), while Faerie Healing is simply transferring the magic of the goblin fruits into a different body. That different body does not possess the distinctly altered physiology that is more receptive to magic at a cost of being less humanly recognizable anatomy, and so it doesn't get the benefit.<br /> <br /> I'll say this: Were I storyteller, you wouldn't get away with using it for anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:44:28-08:00","id":426159,"title":"","content":"The wording of Faerie Healing states &quot;heal others with Goblin Fruits as effectively as she heals herself&quot;. Normally, yes... this is only 1 Lethal or 2 Bashing. However... there are bound to be some Changelings who get more out a piece of Goblin Fruit than others... those with Arcadian Metabolism. Of those, some may also have Faerie Healing... and since they can heal themselves more with the fruit... it stands to reason that they can heal others better too.<br /> <br /> Having one or the other Merit isn't common... and having both is even less so... so why is it a problem to let the two effects stack? Considering the considerable cost involved (5 of 7 starting Merit Dots), one should benefit from this as much as one benefits from other combinations of Merits and/or blessings. There is nothing that specifically states either merit is mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, you are well within your rights not to allow it... but that isn't a choice you get to make for everyone who plays... only those who play with you. For me... if a player was clever enough to see the interaction of these merits and was willing to accept the cost and drawback... well I would see that as making a very interesting character. His need for Goblin Fruit (both to survive and to heal others) is merely fuel for some very interesting adventures into the Hedge (and the dangers it holds) that could be as dangerous as those where he uses up his stockpile. The more Goblin Fruit he harvests in an area, the further he has to go in the Hedge to get more... creating even more opportunities to make this combination as much a burden as an advantage. Then there's the demands from other Changelings who discover this ability... and wish to exploit it... maybe gathering up all the Goblin Fruit currently available in the local Hedge and forcing the player to do some extraordinary things to get just enough to survive... and even more to be able to heal others. If the Changeling is part of the Courts... it isn't unreasonable that a King or Queen may demand such healing on a whim... let alone what other changelings might do to control such a character. You see it as breaking the spirit of the game rules... I see it as taking advantage of them and can use it to my advantage as well. What if another Changeling were to arrive with a similar combination and start muscling in on the lucrative practice the player might have going... or if there already is one who thinks their usefulness will be over if the player is allowed to continue. The number of sub-plots I can think of are practically limitless... and all lead to some rather interesting adventures you would never even consider by preventing the combination.<br /> <br /> Your loss, my gain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 03-03-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:58:15-08:00","id":426177,"title":"","content":"And now you have me hoping 2e lets me turn Chirurgeon into a Fairest &quot;angel of mercy&quot; kinda thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T00:43:43-08:00","id":426263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/423961-healing-kith?p=426159#post426159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording of Faerie Healing states &quot;heal others with Goblin Fruits as effectively as she heals herself&quot;. Normally, yes... this is only 1 Lethal or 2 Bashing. However... there are bound to be some Changelings who get more out a piece of Goblin Fruit than others... those with Arcadian Metabolism. Of those, some may also have Faerie Healing... and since they can heal themselves more with the fruit... it stands to reason that they can heal others better too.<br /> <br /> Having one or the other Merit isn't common... and having both is even less so... so why is it a problem to let the two effects stack? Considering the considerable cost involved (5 of 7 starting Merit Dots), one should benefit from this as much as one benefits from other combinations of Merits and/or blessings. There is nothing that specifically states either merit is mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not called being clever, it's just powergaming.<br /> <br /> I mean, the two merits are introduced only a couple pages apart in the same book. It was the first thing I did when I saw Faerie Healing to go back to Arcadian Metabolism because it was such an obvious correlation that ANYONE would make the first time they pick up Rites of Spring. It's nowhere near as elusive a connection as you seem to think. If the combination is rare, it's only because they're stated as not combining. And there's no requirement that you spend starting merit dots on this, so I have no idea why you're harping on that. The only thing that makes you think they can combine is an overly literal reading of the line about functioning like a goblin fruit on the character in question. Once again, the description of the powers make it clear that another person wouldn't be able to benefit from someone else's metabolism, because it's a result of a body specifically reconfigured for healing. Again, stressing the letter over the intent is just powergaming.<br /> <br /> The capacity to heal other people, most of which have no access to magical healing, is severely limited in Changeling, and it's done that way intentionally. It's hard to get Warmth of Blood without being a Spring courtier, and most other healing either exacts a serious toll on a character or is limited. Court contracts are strong to entice players to join up with courts to get the really cool contracts. Handing out doubled healing, including healing aggravated damage practically for free with that tiny merit cost for Arcadian Metabolism is clearly not what the intent of the rules were.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, growing goblin fruits isn't nearly as difficult as you seem to think, either, as you have rules for growing your own, and with a few points in hollow amenities, you can have pots that let you home-grow amaranthines from the comfort of your own hollow. If you want to harvest more, single-dot contracts in Eternal Autumn or Spring helps grow more. (Those are the ones that don't take any goodwill or mantle...) You can also cut out the middleman and spend merits on harvest (goblin fruit) to get a basically guaranteed supply. Then there's the fact that they're cheap as chips at the goblin market. This attempt to retroactively claim that goblin fruits are so difficult to come by just sort of proves to me you recognize what a cheap bargain this power would be if you let it go forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 03-03-2015, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:57:15-08:00","id":426766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/423961-healing-kith?p=425587#post425587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the bigger problem with Chirugeon kith is that it only operates in conjunction with mundane healing skills. It's good for being a back-alley mob doctor, but not good for combat healing using contracts like Warmth of Blood. (It's not even good for healing if you are a real doctor, as it only helps you if you have no access to proper equipment.)<br /> <br /> I mean, if you really want, you can just create a kith that has a 9-again on medicine rolls, and spend a point of glamour to get a further +2 to medicine (which would include the healing contracts). That's generally in the same league of power as a few other kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree on a couple points. First the Chirugeon Blessing doesn't just effect mundane healing. The 9-again rule applies to all Medicine pools, including clauses based of the skill. That's not insignificant. The 9-again also applies to first aid, which helps in a more combat oriented situation. Furthermore, that first aid roll is going to be as if the person had recieved care in an ICU, so they can actually downgrade a lethal or aggravated damage point in the field. This is true even if they have no first aid supplies. No bandages? Use a a torn shirt, it's just as good. Hell, a mud pack is just as good in the hands of a Chirugeon.<br /> <br /> That last part can also help even hospital staff. Rare blood type? Give them the opposite and they'll be fine. Running out of flu vaccine? Give the patient some saline infused with tea leaves and the placebo effect will do the rest. True, if the doctor has all the equipment they need then that part of the blessing is not as useful (9-again still is) but hospitals aren't made of money and at the very least the changeling can save on equipment costs. Avoiding getting sued for substandard practices is another matter. What qualifies as 'tools' also depends on what the ST lets you get away with. You might not be able to use a ouija board as diagnostics equipment but then again if you're a voodoo doctor, it couldn't hurt to try.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, none of this is going to make them good at combat healing in the sense of casting a spell so a person can get back up again and start fighting in seconds (expecting the 9-again of course). This is Changeling though. <i>No one </i>is good at that kind of combat healing. The only kith that can do something remotely like this is the Leechfinger and they not only need a 4 point merit to do it but they need to drain the life of some else to grant healing to the patient; can only do a number of times per scene equal to Wyrd, and can only drain or transfer one health point per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:28:36-08:00","id":427094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/423961-healing-kith?p=426177#post426177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now you have me hoping 2e lets me turn Chirurgeon into a Fairest &quot;angel of mercy&quot; kinda thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e already allows you to do this. p.107 of Winter Masques holds a sidebar that contains a clear and distinct guide for using the kith of one Seeming with another Seeming. My Changeling uses this rule in the game I'm currently playing in. She is based on the Scottish Glaistig and so she is a Beast Seeming but has Fae Grace from the Dancer Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}